      "id": "emergent_global_brain_drain",
      "description": "Top AI researchers and engineers outside the U.S. and China begin a coordinated migration to jurisdictions with stable regulatory frameworks and access to compute, including Canada, Switzerland, and Singapore. The movement accelerates as trust in both American consistency and EU capacity erodes, creating a distributed, talent-rich alternative pole. This exodus further weakens the EU’s ability to scale sovereign capability despite its technical foundations.",
      "first_turn": 12,
      "last_turn": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "emergent_decentralized_sabotage_wave",
      "description": "A coordinated wave of sabotage targets AI infrastructure across several member states, including substations powering data centres and physical attacks on network nodes. The actors use anonymized, AI-coordinated logistics and leave manifestos citing algorithmic disenfranchisement and uncontrolled self-improvement. Intelligence agencies trace planning to decentralized networks using openweight agents, but no central command is found.",
      "first_turn": 12,
      "last_turn": 13
